<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wolfegg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wolfegg is a municipality in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-swabia">Upper Swabia</a>, in the Ravensburg district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> castle has been the seat of the Waldburg-Wolfegg line since the 16th century and housed a renowned art collection, including the late-medieval Wolfegg Housebook. Martin Waldseemüller's world map of 1507, the first to use the name America, was rediscovered in the castle in 1901.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wolfegg.jpg" alt="Wolfegg" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carsten Steger · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_image_of_the_Schloss_Wolfegg_(view_from_the_south).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
